<title>SOUTH AFRICA: WARBURG TO ADVISE S.AFRICA ON TELECOMMS SELL-OFF.</title>
<headline>WARBURG TO ADVISE S.AFRICA ON TELECOMMS SELL-OFF.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merchant Bank SBC Warburg was appointed on Sunday to advise South Africa's telecommunications ministry on proposed privatisation.</p>
<p>&quot;SBC Warburg will advise on the overall sectoral issues and will interact with Goldman Sachs International, advisors on the preparation of Telkom,&quot; the Ministry of Post, Telecommunications and Broadcasting said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that one of Warburg's tasks would be to evaluate international telecommunications operators who are potential strategic equity partners.</p>
<p>HSBC Investment Bank Plc was awarded the wider tender to advise the government on overall restructuring of state assets last month.</p>
<p>- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
